   * @x-autobe-specification Implement a guest token refresh endpoint that exchanges a valid refresh credential for a new authorization payload. The service should validate the incoming refresh request body defined by ITodoAppGuest.IRefresh, verify the refresh token or session continuation data, and issue a fresh ITodoAppGuest.IAuthorized response. If the underlying guest session record exists, the refresh flow should confirm it is still valid and has not expired or been revoked by application policy.
   *
   * The operation must reject expired, invalid, or structurally incorrect refresh requests. It should be implemented as a public token renewal endpoint that does not require an authenticated member context, but it must still enforce strict validation of the refresh credential before reissuing authorization data.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Post("refresh")
  public async refresh(
    @TypedBody()
    body: ITodoAppGuest.IRefresh,
  ): Promise<ITodoAppGuest.IAuthorized> {
    try {
      return await postTodoAppAuthGuestRefresh({
